  "defects_for_other_owners": [
    "tools/source-library text search matches literally within one line and has no whitespace-tolerant mode, so double-spaced Internet Archive text layers give silent false negatives.",
    "The remote-scan artifact records of PL 107 (1864) and PL 9 (1844) do not name the new tracked facsimile excerpts in their access-limitation notes (shared records, not edited here).",
    "src/sources/inventories/source-family-migration-v1.toml: pinned canonical_catalog_snapshot is stale after the new artifacts; the ledger owner refreshes it.",
    "src/sources/inventories/claude-publications-v1.toml is stale for this document's open revision (hashes and absent synthesis/homily files).",
    "No work records exist for Hilary's In Matthaeum, Bruno of Wuerzburg's Expositio Psalmorum (in PL 142), the PL 151 sacramentary and liturgical excerpts, Peter of Celle (PL 202), or Bernard's In transitu S. Malachiae.",
    "The library holds no Latin of Augustine's Sermons XIX-XXI or De sermone Domini, of Gregory's Moralia, of Cyprian's Ad Fortunatum or of Victorinus, and no text of Jerome's commentary on Matthew to check the source of Rabanus on Mt 11:28.",
    "author-standing-v1.toml lacks rows for Bruno of Wuerzburg, Bernard, Cyprian, Victorinus of Pettau, Bonaventure, Alphonsus Liguori and Peter of Celle.",
    "proper-components.toml (assembly-owned) omits Rabanus Maurus from the carrying authors of the beatitudes lane although research records him as carrying Reading B.",
    "The study's section on the Lord's Prayer and the beatitudes quotes PL 107 lines 93919-93920 as Rabanus's own; the passage is Augustine's De sermone Domini II.11.38 taken over by Rabanus."
  ],
